Third-party components
----------------------

* libsignal (org.signal:libsignal-android) — the Signal protocol implementation
  (X3DH/PQXDH key agreement and the Double Ratchet). Licensed under the GNU
  Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0). Because LegendMessage links
  libsignal, distributing a combined binary places that combination under the
  AGPL's terms for the libsignal portions. LegendMessage is peer-to-peer and
  runs no server that offers the software to users over a network, so the AGPL's
  remote-interaction clause (section 13) has nothing to attach to in normal use.
  GPLv3 and AGPLv3 are mutually compatible by design (each license's section 13).

* ZXing / zxing-android-embedded — QR code generation and scanning.
  Apache License 2.0.

* AndroidX libraries — Apache License 2.0.

* Tor (via info.guardianproject:tor-android and jtorctl), added in Stage 3 —
  Tor is BSD-3-Clause; jtorctl is BSD-3-Clause.
